#### Section Layout

#### multiboot section comes first

- Verify: multiboot section comes first


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 6 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: multiboot section comes first")
# @req: REQ-FEATURE-X86Boot-001
# Multiboot header must be within first 8KB
val MULTIBOOT_ADDR: i64 = 0x00100000
val MULTIBOOT_LIMIT: i64 = 0x00102000  # 8KB after load addr
expect(MULTIBOOT_ADDR).to_be_less_than(MULTIBOOT_LIMIT)
```

</details>

### QEMU Exit Codes

#### Exit Code Translation

#### success exit code (0) becomes (1)

- Verify: success exit code (0) becomes (1)
   - Expected: qemu_exit equals `1)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 6 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: success exit code (0) becomes (1)")
# @req: REQ-FEATURE-X86Boot-001
# QEMU: exit_code = (value << 1) | 1
val value = 0
val qemu_exit = (value << 1) | 1
expect(qemu_exit).to_equal(1)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract
```

</details>

